{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Like laughter, zimah</b> — it is scheming of evils. The meaning of \"like laughter\" — it is easy for the fool to do; so too the act of zimah is easy in his eyes." "<b>But wisdom to a man</b> — he understands that it will guard him from doing zimah; therefore he desires it. Another interpretation: as wisdom to a man of understanding, so the fool rejoices to do zimah."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:56.863964231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}